            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dave"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I rolled the apples in sugar and cinnamon then rolled in creassant rolls",
            "datePublished": "2022-08-03T21:56:35.170Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "QuickHoney2526"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this!! Will tweek next time by baking the apple dumplings on a metal pan and not in sauce to make the bottoms crispy. Used 4 cara cara oranges with lots of crushed orange segments in the juice -- will always keep crushed orange segments in but may reduce amount of butter in sauce. Will serve heated sauce (thickened a bit w/cornstarch) over cooled dumplings. A perfect dessert for brunch and anytime -- just so yummy and easy to prepare!!",
            "datePublished": "2023-03-06T16:57:23.392Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ScratchBakerCR"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good but a bit too sweet for me. I will definitely make it again, but next time I'll reduce the sugar by 1/3 cup. I'll also cut the OJ/butter sauce in half (makes way more than you need!) and add a bit of cornstarch to thicken it up a bit so it's more like a glaze rather than a liquid.",
            "datePublished": "2022-10-16T23:22:05.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lois Hopper"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought the syrup might be a bit thin so I added 1 teaspoon of corn starch to the vanilla, mixed it then added it to the butter, sugar, orange juice after they came to a boil. \nI think a little less sugar could be used for people who don’t want it too sweet. \nI wasn’t sure if it would be too strong an orange flavor but it was perfect. The syrup could be used on many things, ie pancakes, etc. It would just need to be reduced. Do use Granny Smiths, they work best. I took most of the syrup out at 30 minutes and cooked the dough and apples another 10 minutes to make the dough less soggy. Great recipes to make with kids!",
            "datePublished": "2021-11-08T00:22:09.163Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Diane"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was good, as far as ease is concerned! \n I did not like the Orange juice flavor and they were sort of soggy.\nMade it again, used Ginger beer instead of the OJ.\nDid NOT cover with foil as some suggested.\nUsed Pillsbury “Butter Flake” Crescents. \nSprinkled sugar, cinnamon, and a pinch of nutmeg on top of the “bundles”, poured the butter, sugar, juice mix around the casserole instead of on top.\nTurned oven up for last 10 minutes to 375.\nJust took them out of the oven…\nThey look beautiful, browned, and crispy!\nWe shall see…more to come after tasting",
            "datePublished": "2021-10-02T22:32:50.007Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "barron_alexandria"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed this into a peach dumpling recipe. I used one can of sliced peaches in 100% juice from Walmart. Placed 1-2 slices per roll. No OJ just the juice from the peaches. Boiled that with the butter and sugar and added the cinnamon with the mixture when the vanilla was added. Poured over the rolls and sprinkled brown sugar and cinnamon. Covered with aluminum foil for the first 20 min and cooked for 7 min without. PERFECT!",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-22T18:10:06.647Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
